{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793962452,"nonce":"4xdv0bRCK+TpxXjo1MkWsJft4oU=","title":"Collatz raw-interpreter OSR path is much slower than the prewarmed path","message":"Investigate entry/body preparation quality before changing promotion thresholds. Frozen LLVM-enabled binaries, runtime LLVM off, native snapshots preserved. Default 2cd187c7 baseline collatz median is about 141 ms. A symmetric diagnostic with ZYNTAX_DISABLE_WARM_UP=1 takes 246.683 ms baseline and 245.306 ms with the scan-filter candidate. All 42 diagnostic wall samples match PUC Lua 5.4 and pass thermal/load/throttle checks. This setting is allowed by snapshot native_policy and both final traces confirm native placement. It is not a proposed production configuration.\n\nThe diagnostic changes the resumed body/layout: default actual TRACE_INTERP transfers use loop ordinal1 with two live-ins (some captures call the already-native ordinary entry). With prewarming disabled both final traces transfer at ordinal0 with four live-ins. No GC occurs in either arithmetic path. Thus disabling prewarming does NOT hold generated execution/entry shape constant and does not prove the cause of the smaller default build-to-build slowdown.\n\nSource audit: tiered_backend.rs handles Interpreted requests by matching the running body tag. Untiered bodies go through publish_outlined_resume_point when optimize_extra exists; failure to outline falls back to publish_baseline_resume_points on that body. Frames on the prepared tier body use its baseline resume points. beadie_adapter::outlined_resume_point_at runs the supplied optimizer on an outlined function; osr::outline_with_facts can decline when the region reads values absent from its frame/definitions. Verify which branch/layout the raw collatz path takes and compare resumed HIR/CLIF/native code to the default path. Do not assume outlining or optimization is absent without tracing it.\n\nNext work: capture pre/post outlined bodies and explicit rejection reasons without disabling snapshots; optimize valid resumed regions while preserving frame ABI and language results. Keep TieredRuntime interpreter-first and optimize upon tier-up. Do not globally disable prewarming or truncate required optimizer rounds. ZYNTAX_OSR_TRACE currently fails snapshot policy's runtime-only allowlist; use safe TRACE_INTERP/DUMP flags for these controls or address that diagnostic compatibility separately.\n\nEvidence /private/tmp/zyntax-mark-filter/full/nuc/no-warm/{results.json,analysis.json,before.trace,after.trace}; baseline/candidate are frozen in /home/raikage/.cache/zyntax-bench/mark-filter-full-20261105. Related e9e16f2, 5a4ff69 dump identity, 1be184c preparation cost and 53de327 warm-up/OSR overlap. No OSR production change is included in the GC scan-filter candidate.","files":null}]}